## WordPress publishing (GenAI MCP x WordPress)

Publish to WordPress through the REST bridge, using the helper `examples/claude-code/wp.sh`
(or plain curl). The site URL and key are in the environment: `WP_URL`, `WP_API_KEY`.

Rules:
- NEVER print, log, echo or write `WP_API_KEY` anywhere (not in files, commits or replies).
- Always create posts with `"status": "draft"`. Publish (`"status": "publish"`) only when the user says so.
- Before publishing, show the user the title, slug, categories and a short summary and wait for approval.
- Use category paths like `"Japan > Kyoto"` (missing levels are created automatically).
- To update a post, send its `post_id`; only the fields you send change.
- Never call `/delete` or any `/media/*` delete endpoint unless the user explicitly asks.
- Upload images with `wp.sh sideload <url> "<alt text>"`, then pass the returned `id` as `featured_media`.
- Verify the site first with `wp.sh validate` (expects `{"valid":true,...}`).
